{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3d487f157fa9c38f65f19c90f7d8b5624c9d8e739860fff0ed6459160dfe44da","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d5a51a7c95ddda051418e14a5598690f0cd652ca7f35dfb792df998661c994dc"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"text":"The product exposes a CLI including `ocx init`, `start`, `stop`, `service`, `codex-shim install`, `health`, `ready`, `status`, `gui`, plus subcommands for providers, accounts, combos, and v2 surface controls.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3f420b19841d6e0c6f7fa840ccfc05c25f8038b0cf85495c69bc5369fb7c9f1c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_21dea0bf4e41c884f6673047429a7ab2c1302ba6dc5b87a78b48070e49b0eb4f","slc_581d336aeae051d8515ed960b9900301082b85fa06c083fffa63766dae39f476"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"text":"The proxy can manage a ChatGPT account pool for Codex auth: quota-aware routing sends new sessions to the lowest-usage healthy account under quota policy, while existing threads normally keep affinity to their starting account, with rebinding on failover, exclusion, affinity expiry, or 401/403/429 recovery.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4693d1cbb9ea8aaa67cc8aab0d05126d48132d4c15fb33e37ca2106285c5dab6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_40b59e06ea5ff4593c68fa0d889e42fe0d6289425352aad0eb7fb80ada184dd8","slc_a1a960f7e79068ff7917c081a1f37aca62ddc7677aab82b4389aa4b267d8c306"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5","src_c5f404598f275482b8232f9d9e141f38"],"text":"The management API refuses agent-driven star requests with `403 agent_consent_required`, and the CLI suppresses the interactive star prompt when an agent is detected, leaving the decision to the user.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_574a4a9d05c6adc6cee83da3237d13974a067c6eead44a672081af1c207e9bfd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5c51dec4aa9a56be425af0f2ec7252d9f327e90ca6f803bfac34976afb8f7f28"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"text":"Combos provide a single virtual model id with failover or weighted round-robin across providers.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5e4e3312513e7689faceaf727c36469b390712f4042e6640005fdef7df813732","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8b7203147513751f3202af9b7b3b947cb9af5f0626c318fcd93758c8c1d7f45d","slc_9a3113bc16f61d373c3b0f0cdbc5549d16ba1e0e77b960cacc4bce7956354a29","slc_d7e7ea9bc94a73fe811c70d8f62381cb7f80ab3ce1a987dc3e7e3b798c4ecb6e"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"text":"Models are targeted with a `provider/model` syntax (e.g. `codex -m \"anthropic/claude-opus-5\"`); omitting the prefix uses the default provider or name-pattern auto-matching, and inner slashes in provider model ids are aliased to `-`.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_702709e4a1e295802072691dd637512dd7591828f2785eb8c77794f8de98ffb7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_016addac6dbb93ffb2d11f9c8b904d5f6972a2255b90fd55d1a79b5313c0f1ba","slc_56c1646d686937bd42677149c31b41da287a8e00c1ded4c5e2d58658a3ef6939","slc_990045eb3de7a0e42f1fa50796bdc3335cb26b260da0547e16b52c557364be61","slc_9f8d00992e2188a53fa515a0c63b077a6d3db50818873194dfc5becd39e6ac5d"],"source_ids":["src_8a3bad3f83415e2ead5c829da034247f"],"text":"Integration with Codex works by writing Codex-native config and catalog files under CODEX_HOME (config.toml, opencodex.config.toml, opencodex-catalog.json, models_cache.json), so routed models appear in Codex's picker without patching Codex itself.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7cd40746fdc8c97761169b413aa712e807933bf95f18a882b3228b51084b9d72","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5a1ba6dc84188bfa0d341edb02448fcb5c72fc9be841f822f9ea42efbb9a61df","slc_a4329d47c2fba6a3070193cf1ad22c2218e50140173f32596b8eb6d2946b06c9","slc_fd4fabbba8cebdd24445b71c96b97c5e120d344883a2485d59f3ad00b87dd593"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"text":"Repository development practice: source development requires the bun CLI on PATH (separate from the bundled runtime), and contributors run `bun install`, `bun run typecheck`, and `bun run test`; contributor setup lives in CONTRIBUTING.md.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8e15bb6a783e8b1e534381dc9458c5e65d563b6c43a9634ee2555f091ffffdd4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f256017381fb013544f02e633d86db4b9204bbd7c68e02c928e8eea4ae5e9c1c"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"text":"By default the proxy binds to 127.0.0.1 without authentication; binding beyond loopback requires OPENCODEX_API_AUTH_TOKEN, which every client request must carry as the `x-opencodex-api-key` header.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9f4a7a386e93bbe17d59a42945df75697074332dfb854400cce04978625fbc62","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3c927436cd69b8b8d686b6569b233bd9c37dcdef2b78b50fa231cdfa21cb8e52","slc_66b1b28ac16fc014d20f07925f2ba643778f456fbcdca6dc8b9f9d4e71e8757f"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"text":"The package requires Node 18+ and bundles the Bun runtime on npm install, so no separate Bun installation (or WSL on Windows) is needed; supported OSes are macOS, Linux, and Windows x64 with launchd, systemd user units, or Task Scheduler/WinSW respectively.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ace621e3a99791d266c18fbe2e8437a97b2aa7bfda5e41018b2b6228ebbe9e43","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c7be76bdc16b9dcec835edbd1627b520ea77336c650fc9a2f93072e13b635c48","slc_d478fc05e6d2b158c1174c325534a6065ae18f58d91a0ca5e1ddad27b57fe2b0","slc_f54fc4f0ab378635613c53afa387730cb69bf93f6c0562b7c799f1b3eccd2c85"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"text":"The runtime tracks 36 categories of retained process state: 12 byte-accounted stores evicted under a default 256 MiB budget, 4 monitored buffers, 24 state-store registrations with 60s expiry sweeps, and LRU-capped memos; live bytes are inspectable via GET /api/system/memory with the admin token.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e051d2f06c9c6681665a728e2c1e7938c74947be8a01a3bd78a219813f39afea","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0e728925bdd73d243b406cbfb3993bc81c98428454e2fdfe23315b93deb1be61","slc_b6ac7421db014e23d0e2b9bcc435cf83148a51ccc9c0842b2d604a0283fb960e"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"text":"The project warns it is community-maintained and unaffiliated with OpenAI or Anthropic, and that providers such as Anthropic may suspend accounts routing through third-party proxies, so use is at the user's own risk.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f191ab9b9bf78fe94c2d944c012709b165babae3cd0b3163c6e102e2c9493375","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"lidge-jun/opencodex@9f7397ed1582 snapshot 37d187e8e70b0f0a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_12b22e1f2b9602e0f7c45b840f81a6f2c41279d0741aa84c3ef33998665b9905"],"source_ids":["src_a158f48d66a65c32b7711029e4a77da5"],"text":"The proxy serves `GET /healthz` for liveness and an unauthenticated `GET /readyz` returning a sanitized JSON identity; ready returns 200 while pending/failed return 503 with Retry-After: 1.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_073ad5213fb54340a221e6970362e102"}
